From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] viogpu_umd: D3D12 video encoding on Vulkan Video

D3D12 video encoding (the video DDI's extended feature, version 0083_0) for
H.264 Main/High and HEVC Main/Main 10, on the Vulkan device's video encode
queue (NVENC on NVIDIA hosts, through Venus). ffmpeg's h264_d3d12va and
hevc_d3d12va encode; checked against the source (PSNR 42-48 dB at their
defaults, no decoder errors).

vkd3d-proton:
- the video encode queue family and VK_KHR_video_queue, video_encode_queue,
  video_encode_h264/h265 and video_maintenance1 when the device has them;
- NV12/P010 textures get VIDEO_ENCODE_SRC and buffers VIDEO_ENCODE_DST,
  profile-independent, and both are concurrent with the encode family, so the
  application's pictures and bitstream buffers are used as they are;
- the interop lookup of a queue family skipped no absent family (a NULL
  dereference whenever optical flow is missing).

viogpu_umd (umd_video.cpp):
- caps from the Vulkan video capabilities; one decode profile listed
  (unsupported), as the runtime requires on graphics devices;
- encoders and heaps; the heap owns the session, its DPB (a texture array: the
  application's reconstructed pictures only name the slots), parameter sets
  and feedback queries;
- parameter sets with the values the D3D12 video encoding spec has drivers
  expect, plus what ffmpeg writes where it departs from it (8-bit POC LSB when
  the GOP says 0; transform_8x8 for High) and AMP when the encoder forces it
  (probed: NVIDIA does);
- EncodeFrame records Vulkan Video into the list (vkd3d-proton's DXVK interop:
  lists and queues on the encode family); H.264 frame_num as the standard has
  it (ffmpeg passes display order); inputs in another format than the
  profile's (vkd3d-proton's P010 is G16) are copied first;
- ResolveEncoderOutputMetadata reads the feedback query on the CPU once the
  submission finished, before the queue's fence (the encode family has no
  compute to do it on the GPU);
- logging stubs in every video table entry (the runtime wants them all).
---
